# THE CORPUS AUDIO IS NOT SOURCE. `mix.opus` is a 100 MB stream-copy concat of
# the ring's segments and `mix-16k.wav` its 16 kHz decode: both are reproducible
# in one caged command from `history/audio/<day>/` (see README.md and the
# `commands` block of manifest.json), and `history/` itself prunes at 12 h. The
# manifest carries the sha256 of each one, so a rebuilt corpus can be compared
# byte for byte without the bytes living here.
*.opus
*.wav

# The per-60 s speech table is a VIEW of `energy_only.bins` in manifest.json
# (same numbers, different container) -- regenerated by freeze-corpus.py, or
# re-derived from the WAV on disk by restamp-corpus.py when they disagree.
speech-60s.csv

# A live capture track lands here (`capture-discord.py --out`).
capture/

__pycache__/
